I first started playing hack when I was 8 years old.  My friend showed me
the game on his dad's Sun 4.  I was hooked.  I sucked worse than anything,
 but it was the game for me.

I first started playing nethack around version 2.x on my Amiga 500 when I was
17.  I was astounded that the game I had played so long ago had evolved into
something with such depth.  I still sucked :>

I showed a friend of mine the game, and he mastered it.  Savescumming (though
I didn't know the term at the time) gave the best overall view of the route
through the game, though he finally managed a successful ascension without
cheating.  I actually thought that was how it was intended to be played, since
it's motion keys being so close to vi likened it to a unix learning exercise,
and the basic scripting involved in savescumming a logical extension of a
 basic unix lesson.

I learned I was wrong about 5 years ago, after posting possibly my third
savescumming ascension to r.g.r.n.  It was about that posting that people
realized I was savescumming, and I got flamed in the way only r.g.r.n. folks
have the capacity to flame.  I am penitent.

In fact, I am so penitent that I realized the only way I found redeem myself
was for my first real ascension to be in a public forum.  A REAL public forum,
not like the cute nethack.alt.org where my first piddly ascension is likely
not even to make the high score list :>

So here it is folks, my apology to the newsgroup by way of YAFAP in the 2007
devnull tournament.  I have now been playing rougelikes for 25 years, and have
ascended my first character.

Note that I declined ALL Tournament challenges.  I gave it a good go last
year, but remember how I suck?  After 3 weeks of being eaten by Grues, I
decided I really wanted to have a decent run this time :>

Paquita the neutral human Valkyrie has been hacking for about 13 years now.
Her survival was first realized with a set of blessed +4 scale mail found
 in the Dungeons of Doom.  Using strategy culled from my friend Piquan, she
 hacked down until finding the quest portal, then hacking her way back up to
 Sokoban, which she had completed handily in 2006 :>  On the way she found 
an altar on level 7, converted it, and was awarded Mjollnir.

Sokoban yielded an AoR, and that coupled with a decent AC from the <heavy!>
scale mail, gave Paquita the confidence to clean out the Mines.  The dwarvish
Liquor Barn turned out to be at the bottom, as well as (all told) 2 
luckstones, and 2 full sets of candles.

In the meantime Paquita had named Sting and Orcrist, sacrificed enough to

glean Giantslayer, and located a magic lamp in Minetown, which properly rubbed
 
delivered her some GoP.  Unfortunately the wish was a little greedy, so 
instead of blessed rustproof +3 gauntlets of power, she got cursed -3
 gauntlets of power.  Suck.  But it turns out the cursed -3 gauntlets of
 power
will still get you a throwing and returning Mjollnir (once holy water is 
applied), so it wasn't a total wash.

The Quest was supposed to make gratuitous use of Giantslayer, but it turned

out that flinging Mjollnir all over the place makes things pretty clean over
all, as -3 is drowned out by the +20 lightning damage... 
And of course around level 15 I just FIND GoP laying around.  Figures.

There were almost no shops in the dungeon.  One big deli which I robbed with
my kitty Fernando when he was still alive, but other than that, once closed
general store and one 2x2 general store do not a shopping extravoganza make.
Even Minetown has tiny, tiny shops (but they did have a tinning kit...)

I had never got a real game past Medusa before, but with the AoR instead of
the BoHs I always got before, it wasn't that bad.  I opted to use wands of
whatever kills from a distance on the moat creatures, which is normally what
had done me in before.  After that, the castle went pretty easily...I made a
beeline for the towers.  The WoW had only 1 charge, but after 13 years of
reading spoilers, I knew what side my bread was buttered on.  Blessed ?s
o' Charging, blessed fireproof BoH were first (Paquita was feeling the
encumberance hurt).  Then I had a brain fart and went for the Yendorian
Express card (but how many Artifact Weapons were in the game by this point?)
Denied.  SDSM and speed boots finished out the "official" charges, and a
blessed "oLS got the "extra" charge (I needed a security blanket.  It went
unused).

I set up basecamp on level 24...there was a "manned" altar to Tyr there, and
 it was just above medusa, so it worked out.  I decided to forgo my OCD get
 every item in the game for eventual polypiling and let the weapons and armor
 be. Piled up everything else though.

Well armored, Gehennom went pretty smooth.  I have to say though, Hell is
definately the home of the HMO.  I ended up with at LEAST 1 nurse per level,
often 2, and occasionally 3.  This will help explain the ending 514 max hit
points.

At this point I started to get a little wiggy.  Though I often die way more
during full moons than one might typically figure, I concentrated the bulk 
of my post-gehennom energy on the full moon thanksgiving weekend (my wife is
the most tolerant individual in creation).  Odin had conceded Firebrand, but
quickly went for Envoy of Balance, and just pooped out spellbooks after that.
Several runs for holy water and caching of gold, gems, and unused artifacts in
a chest on level 1, plus use of a fortuitous wish on a bless wand of polymorph
put me in business (I had already secured the rest of the armor package).

I gave a bried try at eating rings, but I was too wound up to make a good go
of things.  It was time.  Went up the tower, /oDeath'ed Rodney, grabbed the
book, cursed ?oTeleport got me to the previously marked vibrating square.  I 
was pretty amazed at this point that the adrenaline in a turn based game 
overcame the OCD I normally bring with me;  Performed the invocation ritual
and found the sanctum replete with cockatrices.  Goody.  30 or 40 rubber
chicken incidents later, the amulet is mine.

Going up through gehennom with the amulet and non-genocided disenchanters 
blows.  Anyway, I got through it.  Grabbed my stash on level one and got the
hell out of there.  Used the Orb of Fate to find the portals in the elemental
planes, then went astral.

I opted for conflict going in.  I suck at this, remember? :>  As it happened,
I managed to pick the wrong altars for the whole trip.  Went for Famine, who
I THOUGHT hungried me to the point of losing Con or somthing, but it turned
 out an angry priest had uncursed my BoH, so I went from Burdened to Strained
(yes, I AM a packrat).  I had brought enough /oDeath and /oTeleportation to
make due, though I thought I was a gonner a number of times there.  Death
turns out to be managable if you have 500 HP and +6 vorpal, +6 silver sabre,
plus conflict giving you a whole screenload of unsuspecting alies.  Pestilence
had the annoying habit of resurrecting every other turn, so I was down to the
end of my /s of death by the time I got to the altar of Odin.

Pardon the bullshit iterm is doing to my endgame in these pastes.  I was
a dedicated linux/freebsd desktop guy until the 10th time an X upgrade went
south, and I'm trying OS X on for the time being...

